    "notes": [
      "async reset",
      "RP2040 Basic Support",
      "Flash",
      "Short to hold in reset",
      "VREG_VOUT: int core regulator, 1.1V Can supply DVDD Place 1uF in/out  bypass near pin.",
      "When held low on powerup, flash SS determines boot mode  (HIGH == flash boot, LOW == USB  device)",
      "WE 830108206909:  CFPX-180 model  10 ppm tol, 20ppm stab  CL 8pF",
      "1v1",
      "USB_VDD supplies USB PHY, nominal 3v3. If IOVDD is 3v3, can share supply.  In fact, in this and many applications, IOVDD, USB_VDD and ADC_AVDD are all powered directly from a single 3v3 supply, with the 1v1 digital  core being handle by on-board regulator.",
      "Flash program header Note: should we replace 3v3 with RUN, to be able to reset/hold while updating flash?",
      "Supply bypass, place near 1, 10, 22, 33, 42, 49",
      "Quad SPI requires QE bit in  status register-2 to be set. In this case, ~{WP} becomes  IO2 and ~{HOLD} becomes IO3.",
      "Factory test mode: GND",
      "Rule of thumb  C1, C2 = 2 * CL - 2 * Cstray Using a stray cap of 5pF, gives Cn = 6pF  Into:  CL = (C1 * C2) / (C1 + C2) + Cstray These Cn = 6p give CL = 8pF -- just what we need.",
      "Logic supply, nominally 3v3.",
      "Supply bypass, near 23, 50",
      "Note: SS pulled-up externally, from  bootmode switch"
    ],
